  "findings": [
    "Gene selection and scaling: the 1.6.1 CSV loader with `view_configs` and the v2 `scaledGeneExpression` / `raw[mutations]` `gene_list` options select the same columns in the same order; the standardized expression agrees to the forward class (v2 scales in float32, 1.6.1 in float64). The 1.6.1 class default `view_configs` second entry (expression only) is the `expr` variant. The 1.6.1 methylation preprocessing (StandardScaler + PCA) has no v2 equivalent: `four_views` deviates.",
    "Default hyperparameters (B5): the 1.6.1 class defaults are n_estimators=100, learning_rate=0.1, max_depth=6, num_leaves=63, subsample=0.8, colsample_bytree=0.8, reg_alpha=0, reg_lambda=0, random_state=42, n_jobs=-1. The first grid point of hyperparameters.yaml (what a run uses) is num_leaves=31, subsample=0.8, colsample_bytree=0.6, reg_alpha=0, reg_lambda=0 (max_depth is not in the grid, so 6), on the view_configs expression+mutations. The v2 `lightgbm` predictor defaults and the `MultiViewLightGBM` preset equal that grid point (`preset` variant: identical effective parameters, exact predictions). Both sides pin random_state=42 (a parity step).",
    "`subsample` has no effect in LightGBM unless `subsample_freq` > 0, and neither side sets it, so bagging is never active on either side (the case sets subsample=0.7 and the effective parameters show subsample_freq=0 on both). `colsample_bytree` (feature_fraction) is active and gives identical trees. With the same lightgbm version (4.7.0) on both sides the predictions are exact."
  ],
